# Virtualization

This document describes how virtualization is implemented in the home lab.

## Hypervisor
- Software: Oracle VirtualBox
- Host OS: Windows
- Virtualization type: Type 2 hypervisor


## Virtual Machine 1
## WS 2022-DC01
- Guest OS: Windows Server 2022 (64-bit)
- VM purpose:
  - Application hosting
  - Service isolation
  - SIEM / log analysis
- Resource Allocation:
  - CPUs: 2
  - Memory: 2 GB
  - Storage: 50 GB VDI (dynamically allocated)
- Why VirtualBox:
  - Easy to use for learning
  - Cross-platform support
  - Suitable for desktop-based home lab
  - Adequate for server tasks and SIEM
- Limitations:
  - Depends on host OS uptime
  - Not designed for high availability
  - Lower performance than bare-metal hypervisors


